    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5230" root="جدع" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُدَاعٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>Withered</i> herbage: (S:) or herbage
<i>that is unwholesome to the feeder upon it:</i> (K:)
or <i>tall, unwholesome, and withered.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And hence, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجُدَاعُ</span> signifies (tropical:)  <i>Death:</i> (K, TA:)
written by some ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَدَاعُ</span></b> . (TA.)

